[Full report](recursive_factoring_report.md)

- **PROVED conditional reduction:** \(c=\sqrt{(1+\sqrt2)\theta}\), including stopping times, recursive inputs, restarts, and transcript invariance.
- **PROVED within the size/smoothness model:** minimum exponents \(2/5\) for one level and \(1/3\) for several levels.
- **OPEN:** the corresponding unconditional growing-degree factoring theorem.

The report includes parameter constraints, numerical constants, primary-source citations, and a split-counting lemma removing the \(2^{\omega(N)}\) loss under an explicit cardinality condition.

**Weakest point:** quantitative relation supply for an adaptive descent tree in one growing-degree field.